L1: name: winui-ui-testing
L2: description: "Automated UI testing for Windows desktop apps — generate a batch test script with the `winapp ui` UI Automation harness (WinApp CLI 0.7+), run all tests in one pass, read results. Covers assertions, interactions, keyboard/touch/pen input, file pickers, dialogs, persistence, accessibility, and screenshot/video capture for Win32, WPF, WinForms, and WinUI 3, in Windows Sandbox or locally."
L3: ---
L4: ### Scope and execution boundary
L5: 
L6: `winapp ui` uses Windows UI Automation (UIA), so the AutomationId-based workflow works with any Windows desktop framework, packaged or unpackaged. Skip WinUI-specific binding/dialog advice for other frameworks.
L7: Windows Sandbox keeps synthetic input off the user's desktop; target selection is in Step 1. Discover the installed contract with `winapp run --help`, `winapp target --help`, and `winapp ui <verb> --help`. Use `--on sandbox`, not `--sandbox` or a top-level `sandbox` command. Do not enable Windows features or launch an app without the task's permission.
L8: - Prerequisites and enablement: see `winui-setup`.
L9: - Project builds/publishes execute on the **host**; deployment, app launch, and `ui --on sandbox` execute in the **guest**. Run the batch script below on the host, not inside `target exec` (which would double-route).
L10: - Real input and capture require an unlocked host and a connected, nonminimized Sandbox client. Tree inspection may work while input cannot; a readable tree is not an input-readiness check.
L11: - `winapp target snapshot sandbox --json` is a read-only readiness query: it neither starts nor reconnects a guest. Use it to diagnose readiness rather than probing the user's desktop.
L12: - The persistent guest is shared, not isolation between mutually untrusted workflows. Coordinate with other users; there is no supported `--unique-identity` option. Use separate machines for mutually untrusted work.
L13: - Guest `--debug-output` supports **packaged** apps only.
L14: ### Approach and command discovery
L15: 
L16: Prefer a single scripted batch over a long series of interactive calls. If you wrote the app, use its XAML/source AutomationIds directly; otherwise inspect its current tree and read source for hidden/lazy flyouts and dialogs. Either way, validate a real window/tree before passing an accessibility audit.
L17: Core verbs: `list-windows`, `inspect`, `search`, `get-property`, `get-value`, `wait-for`; `invoke`, `click`, `set-value`, `focus`, `scroll-into-view`; `send-keys`, `hover`, `drag`, `touch`, `pen`; `screenshot`, `record`. Use each verb's `--help` for selectors and options, rather than guessing from this short reference.
L18: ### Step 1: Select a target, then keep the PID and target together
L19: Prefer `sandbox` when Windows Sandbox is available; otherwise tell the user and choose `local`. **If the user explicitly requested Windows Sandbox and it is unavailable, stop** and point them to the enablement steps in `winui-setup`. A stopped guest does not prove unavailability: `target snapshot` can report no running target while the feature is enabled. App build/test failures are not Sandbox unavailability.
L20: The same policy applies to diagnostics: unpackaged apps can't use guest `--debug-output`, so diagnose them locally unless Sandbox was explicitly requested.
L21: Pass the selected target to the template: it launches with `winapp run . --on sandbox --detach --json` for a guest, or omits `--on sandbox` for local execution. Reuse an already-running app only when its captured target matches the selected target and the guest has not been recreated. Never pass a guest PID to default-host `winapp ui`. If a target becomes unavailable after selection, report it and select again under the same policy; the script itself never retries in another target.
L22: The run JSON includes **`ProcessId`**, **`ProcessScope`**, and **`UiTargetArgs`** (PascalCase). In Windows Sandbox, `UiTargetArgs` is **`--on sandbox -a <guestPID>`**: preserve both parts, not just the number. For an explicitly requested **unpackaged** guest run, the launch result has no app PID: launch separately, find the intended app by process/title with target-wide `winapp ui list-windows --on sandbox --json`, then pass its PID with `-Target sandbox -AppPid <PID> -AppScope sandbox`.
L23: Never use the containment PID. A fresh guest invalidates old PIDs/HWNDs.
L24: ### Step 2: Write the host-side batch
L25: 
L26: Create `ui-tests.ps1`, replace the sample AutomationIds/expected values with the app's requirements, and add the relevant examples below **inside the outer `try`**, before its `finally`. The two small command helpers only route and check CLI calls; they do not implement a target manager. Use them for **every** added command so an earlier native failure cannot be hidden by a later success.
L27: ```powershell
L28: # ui-tests.ps1
L29: param(
L30:     [Parameter(Mandatory)][ValidateSet('sandbox', 'local')][string]$Target,
L31:     [int]$AppPid = 0,
L32:     [ValidateSet('sandbox', 'local')][string]$AppScope,
L33:     [ValidateNotNullOrEmpty()][string]$WorkflowId = [guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N'),
L34:     [string]$ArtifactDirectory = (Join-Path '.\ui-test-artifacts' ([guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')))
L35: )
L36: $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
L37: $PSNativeCommandUseErrorActionPreference = $false
L38: $ScopeArgs = @(if ($Target -eq 'sandbox') { '--on'; 'sandbox' })
L39: $previousWorkflowId = $env:WINAPP_UI_WORKFLOW_ID
L40: $env:WINAPP_UI_WORKFLOW_ID = $WorkflowId
L41: $results = [Collections.Generic.List[object]]::new()
L42: $screenshots = [Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()
L43: $uiStarted = $false
L44: function Invoke-WinAppChecked {
L45:     param([string[]]$Arguments)
L46:     $global:LASTEXITCODE = $null
L47:     $output = @(& winapp @Arguments)
L48:     $code = $global:LASTEXITCODE
L49:     if ($null -eq $code -or $code -ne 0) {
L50:         throw "winapp $($Arguments -join ' ') failed (exit $code). $($output -join "`n")"
L51:     }
L52:     $output
L53: }
L54: function Invoke-Ui {
L55:     param([string[]]$Arguments, [string]$Window)
L56:     $selector = if ($Window) { @('-w', $Window) } else { @('-a', "$AppPid") }
L57:     Invoke-WinAppChecked (@('ui') + $Arguments + $ScopeArgs + $selector)
L58: }
L59: 
L60: function Test-UI {
L61:     param([string]$Name, [scriptblock]$Script)
L62:     try {
L63:         & $Script | Out-Null
L64:         $results.Add(@{ name = $Name; status = 'PASS' })
L65:     } catch {
L66:         $results.Add(@{ name = $Name; status = 'FAIL'; detail = "$_" })
L67:     }
L68: }
L69: function Save-Screenshot {
L70:     param([string]$Name)
L71:     $path = Join-Path $ArtifactDirectory $Name
L72:     if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $path) { throw "Choose a new evidence path: $path" }
L73:     Invoke-Ui @('screenshot', '--output', $path) -Window $hwnd | Out-Null
L74:     if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $path -PathType Leaf) -or (Get-Item -LiteralPath $path).Length -eq 0) {
L75:         throw "Screenshot was not delivered to the host: $path"
L76:     }
L77:     $screenshots.Add($path)
L78: }
L79: try {
L80:     $ArtifactDirectory = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath($ArtifactDirectory)
L81:     New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ArtifactDirectory | Out-Null
L82:     if ($AppPid -lt 0) { throw 'AppPid must be positive, or zero to launch.' }
L83:     if ($AppPid -gt 0) {
L84:         if ($AppScope -ne $Target) {
L85:             throw 'Reusing a PID requires matching -AppScope and -Target from the same live target.'
L86:         }
L87:     } else {
L88:         $launch = Invoke-WinAppChecked (@('run', '.') + $ScopeArgs + @('--detach', '--json')) |
L89:             ConvertFrom-Json
L90:         if ($launch.Error -or -not $launch.ProcessId -or [int]$launch.ProcessId -le 0) {
L91:             throw "No app ProcessId. For unpackaged guest runs, discover the app in that target and rerun with -AppPid and -AppScope. $($launch.Error)"
L92:         }
L93:         $AppPid = [int]$launch.ProcessId
L94:         if ($Target -eq 'sandbox' -and
L95:             ($launch.ProcessScope -ne 'sandbox' -or $launch.UiTargetArgs -ne "--on sandbox -a $AppPid")) {
L96:             throw 'Launch response is missing the expected Sandbox ProcessScope / UiTargetArgs pair.'
L97:         }
L98:         if ($Target -eq 'local' -and $launch.ProcessScope -and $launch.ProcessScope -ne 'local') {
L99:             throw 'Launch response belongs to a different target.'
L100:         }
L101:     }
L102:     $uiStarted = $true
L103:     $windows = @(Invoke-Ui @('list-windows', '--json') | ConvertFrom-Json)
L104:     $main = $windows | Where-Object { $_.hwnd -and $_.hwnd -ne '0' -and $_.title -ne 'PopupHost' } |
L105:         Select-Object -First 1
L106:     if (-not $main) { throw 'No app window found in the selected target; rediscover after a fresh guest.' }
L107:     $hwnd = [string]$main.hwnd
L108:     Test-UI 'Initial screenshot delivered' { Save-Screenshot '01-initial.png' }
L109:     Test-UI 'Home exists' { Invoke-Ui @('wait-for', 'NavHome', '-t', '3000') }
L110:     Test-UI 'Navigate to Settings' {
L111:         Invoke-Ui @('invoke', 'NavSettings')
L112:         Invoke-Ui @('wait-for', 'TxtUserName', '-t', '3000')
L113:     }
L114:     Test-UI 'Save username' {
L115:         Invoke-Ui @('set-value', 'TxtUserName', 'TestUser')
L116:         Invoke-Ui @('invoke', 'BtnSave')
L117:         Invoke-Ui @('wait-for', 'TxtUserName', '--value', 'TestUser', '-t', '2000')
L118:     }
L119:     Test-UI 'Default values' {
L120:         Invoke-Ui @('wait-for', 'CmbTheme', '--value', 'System default', '-t', '2000')
L121:         Invoke-Ui @('wait-for', 'TglLogging', '--value', 'Off', '-t', '2000')
L122:     }
L123:     Test-UI 'App controls have AutomationIds' {
L124:         $inspection = Invoke-Ui @('inspect', '--interactive', '--json') -Window $hwnd | ConvertFrom-Json
L125:         function Get-Elements($nodes) {
L126:             foreach ($node in $nodes) {
L127:                 if ($null -ne $node) { $node; Get-Elements $node.children }
L128:             }
L129:         }
L130:         $allElements = @(Get-Elements @($inspection.windows | ForEach-Object { $_.elements }))
L131:         if (-not $allElements.Count) { throw 'Inspection returned no elements; not an accessibility PASS.' }
L132:         $appElements = @($allElements | Where-Object {
L133:             $_.type -match 'Button|TextBox|ComboBox|CheckBox|ToggleSwitch|TabItem|Edit' -and
L134:             $_.name -notmatch 'Minimize|Maximize|Close|System' -and
L135:             $_.className -notmatch 'PickerHost|#32770|CabinetWClass'
L136:         })
L137:         if (-not $appElements.Count) { throw 'No app controls were audited; adjust selectors rather than passing.' }
L138:         $missingId = @($appElements | Where-Object { -not $_.automationId })
L139:         if ($missingId.Count) {
L140:             throw "Missing AutomationIds: $(($missingId | ForEach-Object { "$($_.type) '$($_.name)'" }) -join ', ')"
L141:         }
L142:     }
L143:     Test-UI 'Final screenshot delivered' { Save-Screenshot '02-settings.png' }
L144: } catch {
L145:     $results.Add(@{ name = 'Target setup / test execution'; status = 'FAIL'; detail = "$_" })
L146: } finally {
L147:     try {
L148:         if ($uiStarted) { Invoke-WinAppChecked (@('ui', 'yield') + $ScopeArgs) | Out-Null }
L149:     } catch {
L150:         $results.Add(@{ name = 'Release UI workflow'; status = 'FAIL'; detail = "$_" })
L151:     } finally {
L152:         $env:WINAPP_UI_WORKFLOW_ID = $previousWorkflowId
L153:     }
L154: }
L155: $failed = @($results | Where-Object { $_.status -eq 'FAIL' }).Count
L156: $report = [ordered]@{
L157:     target = $Target; appPid = $AppPid; workflowId = $WorkflowId
L158:     passed = $results.Count - $failed; failed = $failed
L159:     results = @($results.ToArray()); screenshots = @($screenshots.ToArray())
L160: }
L161: $report | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 6 | Set-Content -LiteralPath '.\test-results.json' -Encoding utf8
L162: Write-Host "Passed: $($report.passed) | Failed: $failed | Results: .\test-results.json"
L163: if ($failed) { exit 1 }
L164: exit 0
L165: ```
